==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|а́ккула||dialectal (Northern)}}

===Etymology===
Directly attested since 18th century as {{m|ru|а́ккула}} and {{m|ru|аку́л}}, while derivative {{m|ru|акулий}} is used to describe liver oil of a [[Greenland shark]] in a source going back to late 16th or early 17th century.

Immediate borrowing from rather different {{der|ru|non|hákarl}} (see internal etymology there) is rejected by Anikin, he rather proposes mediation by some {{bor|ru|smi}} language.

Compare dialectal {{cog|no|haakall}}, {{cog|sms|akkli}}, {{cog|sjd|а̄һклэӈӈк}}, {{cog|se|áhkạlakkis|t=Greenland shark}}.

